    <Element Type="Comment" Id="F947E262">
        <Comment>
            The bubble sort algorithm is very simple and straightforward, but also very inefficient and slow.
            It works by repeatedly iterating through the list and comparing two items at a time, swapping them
            if they are in the wrong order. When no more swapping is needed, the list is sorted.
            The following example sorts the Scores array in ascending order.
        </Comment>
    </Element>
