    <Element Type="Comment" Id="83D188D9">
        <Comment>
            The selection sort algorithm is fairly simple and moderately efficient for small lists.
            It works by first finding the smallest element using a linear scan and swapping it into the first position
            in the list. The second smallest element is then found and swapped into the second position in the list, and so on.
        </Comment>
    </Element>
