    <Element Type="Comment" Id="7BB14EE0">
        <Comment>
            The quick sort algorithm is somewhat complex, but is among the fastest sorting algorithms in practice.
            This is a divide and conquer algorithm which relies on a partition operation: we choose an element,
            called a pivot, move all smaller elements before the pivot, and move all greater elements after it.
            These two groups of smaller and greater elements are then subdivided in the same manner. The
            process is repeated until the groups are too small to sort, at which point the list is sorted.
        </Comment>
    </Element>
